Subject: [PATCH] qcacld: compare the hw mode counts as integers

wma_update_mlme_aux_dev_caps() checks that the WMI and MLME hw mode
enums have the same number of entries by comparing their MAX values,
which belong to different enum types. clang 20 rejects that
(-Wenum-compare, -Werror). Compare them as int32_t, as newer
qcacld-3.0 (FP6 modules, lineage-23.2) does; the check is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/qcacld-3.0/core/wma/src/wma_main.c
+++ b/qcacld-3.0/core/wma/src/wma_main.c
@@ -6294,7 +6294,7 @@
 	struct wlan_mlme_aux_dev_caps
 		wlan_mlme_aux0_dev_caps[WLAN_MLME_HW_MODE_MAX] = {0};

-	if (WMI_HOST_HW_MODE_MAX != WLAN_MLME_HW_MODE_MAX)
+	if ((int32_t)WMI_HOST_HW_MODE_MAX != (int32_t)WLAN_MLME_HW_MODE_MAX)
 		wma_err("struct define mismatch, pls fix it.");

 	num_aux_dev_caps =
